※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4613 LANG_ARENA_VALUE_ANSWERED

※ A function that answers something made in an arena it made itself answers something that
※ is gone once it returns: a pure function gives back every arena it made on the way out, and
※ with it everything made there.  An arena the caller handed over is the caller's, and what
※ is made in that one lasts as long as the caller says.

fn joined(first: str) → str:
    let scratch: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(scratch)
    first ⧺ "!" in scratch

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    if joined("a") = "a!": 0u6 else: 1u6
